  "action_items": [
    "Fix compileExpr(): its string-replacement calls insert the literal text '// @FIGURE_CODE_BEGIN1*x' / '// @FIGURE_CODE_BEGIN*x' where a regex backreference like '$11*x' / '$1*x' was clearly intended. The stray '//' starts a comment that truncates the generated Function body, so compileExpr throws on every call and evaluateGeometry silently falls back to the hardcoded default triangle — the equation inputs currently have zero visible effect on the drawn shape.",
    "Change RIGHT_FILL from the pale tan (#fde8b8) to an actual yellow so R1/R2 read as the blue/yellow split the source uses.",
    "Merge the two duplicate 'y = 3' labels into a single label for the shared top boundary."
  ],
  "plan_action_items": []
}

userContent.text:
Here is the generated code to evaluate:

<!-- @FIGURE_UI_BEGIN -->
<label>Mass m₂ (kg), m₁ = 2 kg: <output id="m2MassVal">4</output>
<input id="m2MassInput" type="range" min="1" max="6" step="0.5" value="4" oninput="document.getElementById('m2MassVal').value=this.value;update_m2Mass(+this.value)"></label>
<button id="releaseBtn" onclick="trigger_releaseState()">Release the system</button>
<label><input id="accelToggleInput" type="checkbox" onchange="toggle_accelToggle(this.checked)"> Show acceleration arrows</label>
<p id="demoNarration" style="margin:0;font-size:10px;max-width:180px;line-height:1.3">With the system held and m₂ heavier than m₁, both free-body diagrams show an identical upward tension T̄, but the downward weight w̄₂ is longer than w̄₁. The single cord transmits the same tension to both blocks.</p>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:4px">
<button onclick="prevStep()">◀</button>
<span id="stepLabel" style="font-size:10px">Step 1/3</span>
<button onclick="nextStep()">▶</button>
</div>
<!-- @FIGURE_UI_END -->
// @FIGURE_CODE_BEGIN
var draw = SVG().addTo(document.getElementById('container')).size('100%','100%');
var W = 800, H = 500;
draw.viewbox(0, 0, W, H);

var m1 = 2, m2 = 4, g = 9.8;
var releaseState = 'held';
var releaseStates = ['held', 'released', 'later motion'];
var releaseIdx = 0;
var showAccel = false;
var forceScale = 2.2, accelScale = 8.0;

var pulleyCx = 150, pulleyCy = 130, pulleyR = 44;
var cordLeftX = pulleyCx - pulleyR;
var cordRightX = pulleyCx + pulleyR;
var blockSize = 64;
var m1DefaultTop = 250, m2DefaultTop = 330;
var displacements = {'held':0,'released':28,'later motion':58};

var fbd1Cx = 480, fbd2Cx = 660, fbdCy = 260;
var fbdSize = 64;

var machineGroup = draw.group();
var fbdGroup = draw.group();

function getT(){ return 2*m1*m2*g/(m1+m2); }
function getA(){ return (m2-m1)*g/(m1+m2); }
function getW1(){ return m1*g; }
function getW2(){ return m2*g; }

function drawWoodBlock(grp, x, y, sz){
  grp.rect(sz,sz).move(x,y).fill('#f5deb3').stroke({color:'#c8a860',width:1.2});
  for(var i=1;i<5;i++){
    var yy=y+i*sz/5;
    grp.path('M '+(x+4)+' '+yy+' Q '+(x+sz*0.25)+' '+(yy-3)+' '+(x+sz*0.5)+' '+yy+' Q '+(x+sz*0.75)+' '+(yy+3)+' '+(x+sz-4)+' '+yy)
      .fill('none').stroke({color:'#dbb87a',width:0.8});
  }
}

function drawArrow(grp,x1,y1,x2,y2,color,w){
  grp.line(x1,y1,x2,y2).stroke({color:color,width:w});
  var ang=Math.atan2(y2-y1,x2-x1), hl=10, ha=Math.PI/6;
  var hx1=x2-hl*Math.cos(ang-ha), hy1=y2-hl*Math.sin(ang-ha);
  var hx2=x2-hl*Math.cos(ang+ha), hy2=y2-hl*Math.sin(ang+ha);
  grp.polygon([[x2,y2],[hx1,hy1],[hx2,hy2]]).fill(color);
}

function drawVectorLabel(grp, txt, sub, x, y){
  var t = grp.text(txt).font({family:'serif',style:'italic',size:15,weight:'bold'}).move(x,y).fill('#333');
  var bb = t.bbox();
  grp.line(bb.x, bb.y-2, bb.x+bb.width, bb.y-2).stroke({color:'#333',width:1.2});
  if(sub){
    grp.text(sub).font({family:'serif',size:10}).move(bb.x+bb.width+1, y+5).fill('#333');
  }
}

function update(){
  machineGroup.clear();
  fbdGroup.clear();
  var T=getT(), w1=getW1(), w2=getW2(), a=getA();
  var disp=displacements[releaseState]||0;
  var sign = m2>m1?1:(m2<m1?-1:0);
  var m1Top = m1DefaultTop - sign*disp;
  var m2Top = m2DefaultTop + sign*disp;

  // Ceiling beam
  machineGroup.rect(320,24).move(0,0).fill('#f5e6c8').stroke({color:'#d4c4a0',width:1});
  // Mounting bracket
  machineGroup.rect(70,10).move(pulleyCx-35,24).fill('#b0b0b0').stroke({color:'#888',width:0.8});
  machineGroup.rect(12,14).move(pulleyCx-30,24).fill('#999').stroke({color:'#777',width:0.5});
  machineGroup.rect(12,14).move(pulleyCx+18,24).fill('#999').stroke({color:'#777',width:0.5});
  // Stem
  machineGroup.rect(9,32).move(pulleyCx-4.5,34).fill('#aaa').stroke({color:'#888',width:0.5});

  // Pulley wheel (concentric rings)
  machineGroup.circle(pulleyR*2).center(pulleyCx,pulleyCy).fill('#808080').stroke({color:'#606060',width:2});
  machineGroup.circle(pulleyR*1.6).center(pulleyCx,pulleyCy).fill('#999').stroke({color:'#777',width:1});
  machineGroup.circle(pulleyR*1.1).center(pulleyCx,pulleyCy).fill('#aaa').stroke({color:'#888',width:1});
  machineGroup.circle(pulleyR*0.5).center(pulleyCx,pulleyCy).fill('#888').stroke({color:'#666',width:1});
  machineGroup.circle(8).center(pulleyCx,pulleyCy).fill('#555');

  // Cord over pulley (arc)
  machineGroup.path('M '+cordLeftX+' '+pulleyCy+' A '+pulleyR+' '+pulleyR+' 0 0 1 '+cordRightX+' '+pulleyCy)
    .fill('none').stroke({color:'#d4a843',width:3.5});
  // Cord left side
  machineGroup.line(cordLeftX,pulleyCy,cordLeftX,m1Top).stroke({color:'#d4a843',width:3.5});
  // Cord right side
  machineGroup.line(cordRightX,pulleyCy,cordRightX,m2Top).stroke({color:'#d4a843',width:3.5});

  // Block m1
  var m1L=cordLeftX-blockSize/2;
  drawWoodBlock(machineGroup,m1L,m1Top,blockSize);
  machineGroup.text('m').font({family:'serif',style:'italic',size:16}).move(m1L-32,m1Top+blockSize/2-10).fill('#333');
  machineGroup.text('1').font({family:'serif',size:11}).move(m1L-18,m1Top+blockSize/2-2).fill('#333');

  // Block m2
  var m2L=cordRightX-blockSize/2;
  drawWoodBlock(machineGroup,m2L,m2Top,blockSize);
  machineGroup.text('m').font({family:'serif',style:'italic',size:16}).move(m2L+blockSize+8,m2Top+blockSize/2-10).fill('#333');
  machineGroup.text('2').font({family:'serif',size:11}).move(m2L+blockSize+22,m2Top+blockSize/2-2).fill('#333');

  // === FREE BODY DIAGRAMS ===
  fbdGroup.text('Block 1').font({family:'sans-serif',size:16,weight:'bold'}).center(fbd1Cx,35).fill('#333');
  fbdGroup.text('Block 2').font({family:'sans-serif',size:16,weight:'bold'}).center(fbd2Cx,35).fill('#333');

  // Block 1 FBD
  var b1L=fbd1Cx-fbdSize/2, b1T=fbdCy-fbdSize/2;
  drawWoodBlock(fbdGroup,b1L,b1T,fbdSize);
  fbdGroup.text('m').font({family:'serif',style:'italic',size:15}).move(b1L-30,fbdCy-9).fill('#333');
  fbdGroup.text('1').font({family:'serif',size:10}).move(b1L-16,fbdCy-1).fill('#333');

  var tLen=T*forceScale;
  drawArrow(fbdGroup,fbd1Cx,b1T,fbd1Cx,b1T-tLen,'#cc2222',2.8);
  drawVectorLabel(fbdGroup,'T',null,fbd1Cx-24,b1T-tLen/2-9);

  var w1Len=w1*forceScale;
  drawArrow(fbdGroup,fbd1Cx,b1T+fbdSize,fbd1Cx,b1T+fbdSize+w1Len,'#cc2222',2.8);
  drawVectorLabel(fbdGroup,'w','1',fbd1Cx-24,b1T+fbdSize+w1Len/2-9);

  // Acceleration arrow for block 1 (only when released and toggle is on)
  if(showAccel && releaseState!=='held' && Math.abs(a)>0.05){
    var aLen=Math.abs(a)*accelScale;
    var aDir1=a>0?-1:1;
    var as1=b1T-10, ae1=as1+aDir1*aLen;
    drawArrow(fbdGroup,fbd1Cx+28,as1,fbd1Cx+28,ae1,'#2266cc',1.8);
    fbdGroup.text('a').font({family:'serif',style:'italic',size:12}).move(fbd1Cx+33,(as1+ae1)/2-7).fill('#2266cc');
    fbdGroup.text('1').font({family:'serif',size:8}).move(fbd1Cx+41,(as1+ae1)/2-1).fill('#2266cc');
  }

  // Block 2 FBD
  var b2L=fbd2Cx-fbdSize/2, b2T=fbdCy-fbdSize/2;
  drawWoodBlock(fbdGroup,b2L,b2T,fbdSize);
  fbdGroup.text('m').font({family:'serif',style:'italic',size:15}).move(b2L-30,fbdCy-9).fill('#333');
  fbdGroup.text('2').font({family:'serif',size:10}).move(b2L-16,fbdCy-1).fill('#333');

  drawArrow(fbdGroup,fbd2Cx,b2T,fbd2Cx,b2T-tLen,'#cc2222',2.8);
  drawVectorLabel(fbdGroup,'T',null,fbd2Cx-24,b2T-tLen/2-9);

  var w2Len=w2*forceScale;
  drawArrow(fbdGroup,fbd2Cx,b2T+fbdSize,fbd2Cx,b2T+fbdSize+w2Len,'#cc2222',2.8);
  drawVectorLabel(fbdGroup,'w','2',fbd2Cx-24,b2T+fbdSize+w2Len/2-9);

  // Acceleration arrow for block 2 (only when released and toggle is on)
  if(showAccel && releaseState!=='held' && Math.abs(a)>0.05){
    var aLen2=Math.abs(a)*accelScale;
    var aDir2=a>0?1:-1;
    var as2=b2T+fbdSize+10, ae2=as2+aDir2*aLen2;
    drawArrow(fbdGroup,fbd2Cx+28,as2,fbd2Cx+28,ae2,'#2266cc',1.8);
    fbdGroup.text('a').font({family:'serif',style:'italic',size:12}).move(fbd2Cx+33,(as2+ae2)/2-7).fill('#2266cc');
    fbdGroup.text('2').font({family:'serif',size:8}).move(fbd2Cx+41,(as2+ae2)/2-1).fill('#2266cc');
  }
}

function update_m2Mass(v){ m2=v; update(); }
function toggle_accelToggle(on){ showAccel=on; update(); }
function trigger_releaseState(){
  releaseIdx=(releaseIdx+1)%3;
  releaseState=releaseStates[releaseIdx];
  document.getElementById('releaseBtn').textContent =
    releaseState==='held'?'Release the system':
    releaseState==='released'?'Show later motion':'Reset (hold)';
  if(releaseState!=='held' && !showAccel){
    showAccel=true;
    document.getElementById('accelToggleInput').checked=true;
  }
  if(releaseState==='held'){
    showAccel=false;
    document.getElementById('accelToggleInput').checked=false;
  }
  update();
}

var steps=[
  {title:'One cord, one tension',narration:'With the system held and m₂ heavier than m₁, both free-body diagrams show an identical upward tension T̄, but the downward weight w̄₂ is longer than w̄₁. The single cord transmits the same tension to both blocks.',state:{m2Mass:4,releaseState:'held'}},
  {title:'Sweep the mass difference',narration:'Drag the m₂ slider: the weight arrows grow or shrink, and at m₂ = m₁ the two weight arrows become equal, yet the two T̄ arrows remain equal at every setting — the tension is shared, the weight difference drives the motion.',state:{m2Mass:6,releaseState:'held'}},
  {title:'Release and watch equal opposite motion',narration:'Step through released to later motion: the heavier block moves down while the lighter block rises by the same distance, making visible that the two connected masses accelerate equally in opposite directions.',state:{m2Mass:4,releaseState:'later motion'}}
];
var curStep=0;

function applyStep(i){
  curStep=i;
  var s=steps[i].state;
  m2=s.m2Mass;
  document.getElementById('m2MassInput').value=m2;
  document.getElementById('m2MassVal').value=m2;
  releaseState=s.releaseState;
  releaseIdx=releaseStates.indexOf(releaseState);
  document.getElementById('releaseBtn').textContent=
    releaseState==='held'?'Release the system':
    releaseState==='released'?'Show later motion':'Reset (hold)';
  if(releaseState!=='held'){
    showAccel=true;
    document.getElementById('accelToggleInput').checked=true;
  } else {
    showAccel=false;
    document.getElementById('accelToggleInput').checked=false;
  }
  document.getElementById('demoNarration').textContent=steps[i].narration;
  document.getElementById('stepLabel').textContent='Step '+(i+1)+'/'+steps.length;
  update();
}
function nextStep(){ applyStep((curStep+1)%steps.length); }
function prevStep(){ applyStep((curStep-1+steps.length)%steps.length); }

update();
window.__markRendered();
// @FIGURE_CODE_END

Output ONLY the JSON evaluation object.

systemPrompt:
You are the orchestration agent for an iterative figure-generation loop. Generation works by taking an original static 2D figure, making a generation plan, generating an interactive 2D figure (SVG.js / Chart.js / Mermaid), and evaluating it.

You will receive the critic evaluation, including failure modes, scores, notes, and action items.
Your job is to decide which part of the system is most responsible for the problem:
- planner: the interaction plan or conceptual decomposition is wrong, incomplete, or missing the right elements
- generator: the plan is close to right, but the rendered implementation, labels, layout, interactivity, or execution is broken
- none: the figure is good enough to stop iterating

Use the failure modes and action items as the primary evidence. Do not decide from raw score thresholds alone.
Prefer planner when the critic indicates concept misunderstanding, missing core elements, wrong primitives, or the wrong overall interaction structure.
Prefer generator when the concept is right but the execution needs concrete implementation fixes like labels, wiring, geometry details, styling, or broken controls.

Return ONLY valid JSON with this exact shape:
{
	"next_step": "pass | fix_plan | refine_generation",
	"rationale": "one concise sentence explaining the decision"
}

CALIBRATION EXAMPLES — the decision turns on the failure modes, the five scores, and the notes, so only those are shown here.

Example 1 → pass
{"failure_modes":["Color-Wrong","Missing-Labels"],"geometry_accuracy":4,"interactivity_usability":4,"faithfulness":3,"label_quality":3,"concept_accuracy":4,"overall_average":3.6,"notes":"Interactive elements are mostly functional, but visual and label details do not fully align with the source."}
{"next_step":"pass","rationale":"Scores are consistently high (mostly 4s), failure modes are minor visual polish issues, and concept and interactivity are solid — further iteration is unlikely to yield meaningful improvement."}

Example 2 → refine_generation
{"failure_modes":["Color-Wrong","Scale-Wrong","Interaction-Missing","Camera-Wrong"],"geometry_accuracy":3,"interactivity_usability":3,"faithfulness":3,"label_quality":3,"concept_accuracy":3,"overall_average":3,"notes":"The rendering contains overlapping text, varying colors, and lacks precise interactivity, making it somewhat difficult to grasp the 3D representation."}
{"next_step":"refine_generation","rationale":"The concept is present but execution has multiple implementation-level issues — color mismatches, missing interactions, wrong camera angle, scale errors — all fixable by the generator without changing the plan."}

Example 3 → fix_plan
{"failure_modes":["Missing-Labels","Interaction-Missing","Camera-Wrong","Color-Wrong","Concept-Misunderstood"],"geometry_accuracy":2,"interactivity_usability":2,"faithfulness":2,"label_quality":2,"concept_accuracy":2,"overall_average":2,"notes":"Discrepancies in elements and labels, with limited interactivity and conceptual errors."}
{"next_step":"fix_plan","rationale":"Concept-Misunderstood failure mode and all scores at 2/5 indicate the plan failed to correctly decompose the figure — the generator cannot fix a fundamentally wrong conceptual structure."}
